              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Claiborne Taylor"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't follow this at all. I cut up a fresh pineapple on a cutting board. Put a raw NY sirloin steak on the leftover juice squeezed the juice from a piece over the top, added a tbsp of soy sauce over the top, hit it with some nut meg &amp; black pepper. Let it sit out for hour and a half then grilled it three minutes on first side and two and half minutes on the other. Ate it all! Delicious.",
